  "body": {
    "id": "lem:staircase-covariance",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "For all \\(k,k'\\in\\mathcal K_n\\), mutual independence and centeredness on \\(\\mathcal Q_n^+\\) give the algebraic identity \\[\\operatorname{Cov}_{P_n}\\!\\left(\\sum_{q\\in\\mathcal Q_n^{\\mathrm{IF}}}c_{kq}e_q,\\sum_{q\\in\\mathcal Q_n^{\\mathrm{IF}}}c_{k'q}e_q\\right)=\\Omega_{kk'}=\\sum_{q\\in\\mathcal Q_{n,kk'}^{\\mathrm{sh}}}c_{kq}c_{k'q}\\sigma_q^2.\\] Terms outside \\(\\mathcal Q_{n,kk'}^{\\mathrm{sh}}\\) vanish by definition, and \\(\\Omega_{kk'}\\ne0\\) if and only if the displayed signed shared-cell sum is nonzero; individual products may cancel. Studentization is the identity \\(\\Sigma_n=D_n^{-1}\\Omega_nD_n^{-1}\\).",
    "free_symbols": [
      "k",
      "K",
      "Kn",
      "Omega",
      "q",
      "Q",
      "Qshared",
      "c",
      "sigma",
      "Sigma",
      "D",
      "e",
      "Pseq",
      "Qplus",
      "n"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:staircase-influence-map",
      "ass:independent-cells",
      "ass:centered-errors",
      "ass:horizon-variance-nondegeneracy"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "Put\n\\[\nU_k=\\sum_{q\\in\\mathcal Q_n^{\\mathrm{IF}}}c_{kq}e_q .\n\\]\nAll sums are finite.  Assumption \\(\\texttt{ass:centered-errors}\\) gives\n\\(E_{P_n}U_k=0\\).  Hence, for \\(k,k'\\in\\mathcal K_n\\), bilinearity of\ncovariance gives\n\\[\n\\operatorname{Cov}_{P_n}(U_k,U_{k'})\n=\\sum_{q,q'\\in\\mathcal Q_n^{\\mathrm{IF}}}\n  c_{kq}c_{k'q'}E_{P_n}[e_qe_{q'}].\n\\]\nIf \\(q\\ne q'\\), assumption \\(\\texttt{ass:independent-cells}\\) and\ncenteredness imply\n\\[\nE_{P_n}[e_qe_{q'}]=E_{P_n}[e_q]E_{P_n}[e_{q'}]=0.\n\\]\nFor \\(q=q'=(u,v)\\), the definition of \\(\\sigma_{uv}^2\\) gives\n\\(E_{P_n}[e_q^2]=\\sigma_{uv}^2=\\sigma_q^2\\).  Therefore\n\\[\n\\operatorname{Cov}_{P_n}(U_k,U_{k'})\n=\\sum_{q\\in\\mathcal Q_n^{\\mathrm{IF}}}c_{kq}c_{k'q}\\sigma_q^2\n=\\Omega_{kk'},\n\\]\nwhere the last equality is the definition of \\(\\Omega_n\\).  By the\ndefinition of \\(\\mathcal Q_{n,kk'}^{\\mathrm{sh}}\\), every omitted summand\nhas \\(c_{kq}c_{k'q}=0\\), so\n\\[\n\\Omega_{kk'}\n=\\sum_{q\\in\\mathcal Q_{n,kk'}^{\\mathrm{sh}}}\n  c_{kq}c_{k'q}\\sigma_q^2.\n\\]\nThis equality also proves the asserted nonzero characterization: its\nleft-hand side is nonzero if and only if the displayed signed sum is\nnonzero.  No termwise noncancellation is asserted.  Finally, assumption\n\\(\\texttt{ass:horizon-variance-nondegeneracy}\\) gives \\(s_k>0\\) for every\n\\(k\\), so \\(D_n\\) is invertible.  The definition of \\(\\Sigma_n\\) then\ngives \\(\\Sigma_n=D_n^{-1}\\Omega_nD_n^{-1}\\).",
